**Root cause confirmed:** Both leaf routers receive two valid eBGP paths to the remote leaf subnet (one via `spine_router_0_0`, one via `spine_router_0_1`) but `maximum-paths` is not configured. FRR BGP's default is single-best-path; `spine_router_0_0` always wins because its router-ID (`172.16.0.1`) beats `spine_router_0_1`'s (`172.16.0.3`). The `eth1` uplinks on both leaves carry zero leaf-to-leaf forwarding traffic. Connectivity still works because the single selected spine is healthy — the user's "cannot reach" complaint is not currently observable — but the ECMP fabric is entirely inoperative.

=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: leaf_router_0_0, leaf_router_0_1
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** BGP multipath (ECMP) configuration in FRR's `address-family ipv4 unicast` on both leaf routers.

**Mechanism:** In a dc_clos_bgp Clos fabric, each leaf router has two equal-cost eBGP uplinks — one to `spine_router_0_0` (ASN 65100) and one to `spine_router_0_1` (ASN 65101). Both spines propagate the remote leaf prefix with identical AS-path length (2 hops), so the routes are genuinely equal-cost. However, without `maximum-paths 2` (or `maximum-paths ebgp 2`) configured under `address-family ipv4 unicast`, FRR installs only the single BGP best path. BGP best-path tiebreaker falls through to lowest neighbor router-ID: `spine_router_0_0` (router-ID `172.16.0.1`) always beats `spine_router_0_1` (`172.16.0.3`). Both leaf routers therefore hard-pin all traffic through `spine_router_0_0` and the `eth1` links to `spine_router_0_1` carry no leaf-to-leaf forwarding traffic at all.

**Localization:** `leaf_router_0_0` (ASN 65200) and `leaf_router_0_1` (ASN 65201) — confirmed by `frr_show_ip_route` (single FIB entry each) and `frr_show_running_config` (no `maximum-paths` present under any address-family).

**Root cause:** `maximum-paths` is absent from the BGP address-family on both leaf routers, disabling ECMP across the dual-spine Clos fabric. Connectivity is intact only because the one selected spine (`spine_router_0_0`) is healthy.

**Fix:** On both `leaf_router_0_0` and `leaf_router_0_1`, add `maximum-paths 2` (or `maximum-paths ebgp 2`) under `address-family ipv4 unicast` in FRR, then reload BGP so both spine paths are installed as equal-cost FIB entries.
=== END ===